+def _share_session_is_live(payload: dict, token: str) -> bool:
+    """True while the snapshot's conversation still exists and holds its token.
+
+    A public link used to outlive its conversation: deleting a session removed
+    the sidecar and never touched the snapshot, so ``/share/<token>`` kept
+    serving the transcript. The sidecar is the authority -- it is removed with
+    the conversation, and a revoke clears its ``share_token`` -- so a snapshot
+    whose session is gone, or has moved on to a newer link, is dead even when no
+    revoke ever reached this store. That also closes the links earlier deletes
+    orphaned. The token comes from the snapshot, or from the request for a
+    snapshot written before it recorded one.
